SUMMARY:North York Central Library\, Emancipation Month: Nature's Enduring Gifts
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Emancipation Month with a musical and interactive presentation! \nLed by Frances Greenidge\, Nature’s Enduring Gifts is an organic retelling of the impact of the American folksong\, Follow the Drinking Gourd\, used by fugitive slaves in the mid-1800s to remember and follow the clues in nature as they journeyed toward freedom in Canada along the Underground Railroad. \nSpace is limited; online registration is encouraged
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/north-york-central-library-emancipation-month-natures-enduring-gifts/
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, 5120 Yonge Street\, North York\, Ontario\, Canada
END:VEVENT
